{"name":"Swimming","hex":"#c2e5e5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"swimming","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act or art of sustaining and propelling the body in water."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state of being dizzy or in vertigo."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swimming"}],"entries":[{"title":"Swimming","blocks":[{"text":"Swimming is the self-propulsion of a person through water, usually for recreation, sport, exercise, or survival. Swimmers achieve locomotion by coordinating limb and body movements to achieve a level of buoyancy and hydrodynamic thrust that results in directional motion. For example, they float to a greater or lesser extent, and move in a given direction by coordinating their forward thrusting actions, especially of their head and torso, with other actions such as stroking with their arms and kicking with their legs. Swimming is a whole body exercise that requires endurance, skill and efficient techniques to maximize speed and minimize energy consumption."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/40._Schwimmzonen-_und_Mastersmeeting_Enns_2017_100m_Brust_Herren_USC_Traun-9897.jpg/330px-40._Schwimmzonen-_und_Mastersmeeting_Enns_2017_100m_Brust_Herren_USC_Traun-9897.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swimming"},{"title":"Swimming (Mac Miller album)","blocks":[{"text":"Swimming is the fifth studio album by American rapper Mac Miller. It was released on August 3, 2018, by REMember Music and Warner Bros. Records. Miller produced the album himself, with Jon Brion, Dev Hynes, J. Cole, ID Labs, Dâm-Funk, DJ Dahi, Tae Beast, Flying Lotus, and Cardo, among others. The album has no credited features, but contains vocal contributions from Dâm-Funk, Dev Hynes, Snoop Dogg, Syd, Thundercat, and JID. Miller died on September 7, 2018, just over a month after Swimming was released, making Swimming the final album released during Miller's lifetime."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5e/Mac_Miller_-_Swimming.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swimming_(Mac_Miller_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Participants_with_the_Water_Warrior_class_perform_squats_prior_to_entering_the_pool_at_Camp_Foster%2C_Okinawa%2C_Japan%2C_July_6%2C_2011_110706-M-VD776-004_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Participants_with_the_Water_Warrior_class_perform_squats_prior_to_entering_the_pool_at_Camp_Foster%2C_Okinawa%2C_Japan%2C_July_6%2C_2011_110706-M-VD776-004_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Participants_with_the_Water_Warrior_class_perform_squats_prior_to_entering_the_pool_at_Camp_Foster%2C_Okinawa%2C_Japan%2C_July_6%2C_2011_110706-M-VD776-004_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Swimmers perform squats prior to entering the pool in a U.S. military base, 2011.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AParticipants_with_the_Water_Warrior_class_perform_squats_prior_to_entering_the_pool_at_Camp_Foster%2C_Okinawa%2C_Japan%2C_July_6%2C_2011_110706-M-VD776-004_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Childrens_are_swimming_%28b%29.jpg/500px-Childrens_are_swimming_%28b%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Childrens_are_swimming_%28b%29.jpg/1280px-Childrens_are_swimming_%28b%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_con